✅ Testing Checklist
Test 1 – Annual Budget
Create an annual budget for FY 2026–2027.
Add department and account-wise budget lines.
Test 2 – Budget Monitoring
Record expenses through the Expense module.
Verify Actual Spend updates automatically from the General Ledger.
Test 3 – Budget Transfer
Transfer AED 5,000 from the Marketing budget to the IT budget.
Ensure transfer history is preserved and total budget remains unchanged.
Test 4 – Budget Revision
Create a new budget revision.
Increase the Travel budget.
Confirm the original version remains unchanged.
Test 5 – Variance Analysis
Compare Budget vs Actual.
Verify:
Variance amount
Variance %
Color indicators (green/yellow/red)
Test 6 – Dashboard
Confirm dashboard widgets accurately reflect:
Total Budget
Actual Spend
Remaining Budget
Departments exceeding budget
Architectural recommendation before F8

At this point, your finance system has enough maturity that it's worth introducing a Notification & Alert Engine (shared across the ERP, not finance-specific). This engine can notify users about:

Budget thresholds exceeded
Overdue customer invoices
Upcoming vendor payments
Bank reconciliation pending
Approval requests
Financial year closing reminders
Low inventory
Asset warranty expiry

Making notifications a shared service now will allow every future module to use a consistent alert mechanism instead of implementing its own notification logic.